{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/501475-inspirational-movies-and-tv-episodes","id":501475,"title":"Inspirational Movies and TV Episodes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-03T01:00:32-07:00","id":501475,"title":"Inspirational Movies and TV Episodes","content":"I decided to start this thread because I like finding new things that fit within the vein of WoD, and because I've had problems finding certain aspects of WoD in Movies/TV in the past (Specifically Werewolf the Forsaken 1e when dealing with Spirits and the Shadow realm).<br /> <br /> So name the Movie or TV Episodes/Series and what you think it could inspire for. Include Spoiler tags if you think the &quot;what&quot; will spoil your enjoyment.<ul><li><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt1905040/\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Pass</a>, <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">God Machine infrastructure</div></div> </div> </div></li> <li><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt4425202/\" target=\"_blank\">Grimm, Mishipeshu</a>, Spirits</li> <li><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0470752/\" target=\"_blank\">Ex Machina,</a> Promethean, The Unfleshed</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 05-03-2015, 04:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T11:57:15-07:00","id":501963,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Manga/GhostHunt\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Hunt</a>, Hunter, psychic phenomena<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T04:54:19-07:00","id":502775,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ParaNorman\" target=\"_blank\">ParaNorman</a>, Sin-Eater/Medium","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T06:05:24-07:00","id":502828,"title":"","content":"<i>Buffy the Vampire Slayer</i> for Mortals or Hunter.<br /> <br /> <i>Gate Keepers 21</i> for a Psychics game (<i>Gate Keepers</i> is too happy for WoD, the sequel OVAs are much darker).<br /> <br /> The currently airing series <i>Kekkai Sensen</i> is a pretty cool setting for when the veil of ignorance is torn asunder.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T16:12:50-07:00","id":503593,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thirteen_Ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Thirteen Ghosts</a>: excellent inspiration for coming up with Geister that have creepy appearances and creepy back stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T17:04:04-07:00","id":503631,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=6&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0CDwQFjAF&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FPerson_of_Interest_%2528TV_series%2529&amp;ei=rwhIVYr9BITEggSTqYCADA&amp;usg=AFQjCNErpGxF1UYywYbiuFXq0MJGZ0v30A&amp;sig2=s8wujO9rAPiMCyzITvEf7w&amp;bvm=bv.92291466,d.eXY\" target=\"_blank\">Person of Interest</a>: Demon, especially Season 4","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T17:27:52-07:00","id":503646,"title":"","content":"Whenever my friends talk about Supernatural we seem to be able to compare notes between that and New World of Darkness. So I guess thats some recommended viewing right there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T20:32:25-07:00","id":503756,"title":"","content":"Shows like the X-Files and Fringe obviously make for good GMC fodder, both featuring examples of technology so advanced it might as well be magic.<br /> <br /> It's not a movie or TV show, but David Mitchell's book <i>The Bone Clocks</i> has a brilliant Demon vibe. In the background of one woman's life is a clandestine battle between two rival groups of immortals, including everything from cover identities to bombs in the mail to occult machinery, with a major plot point being something tantamount to a Soul Pact.<br /> <br /> More than the specifics though, the general feeling of seeing glimpses of a supernatural conflict from the mortal perspective is a great example of what, presumably, every mortal in the World of Darkness must go through. Since the second edition has started bandying around the idea that all humans have had contact with the supernatural but refuse to acknowledge it, it's interesting to see an example of what that might look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T05:18:46-07:00","id":504060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/501475-inspirational-movies-and-tv-episodes?p=503646#post503646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whenever my friends talk about Supernatural we seem to be able to compare notes between that and New World of Darkness. So I guess thats some recommended viewing right there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>So much so that it was mentioned in the Inspirations section of HtV.<br /> <br /> I know it's actually a game, but there's the Mask of the Betrayer Expansion for NWN2, which seems like a very good example of a low-Synergy Sin-Eater with an asshole Geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T06:04:04-07:00","id":504092,"title":"","content":"Also a Book, But i think it Could be a definite inspiration for GMC; Daemon by David Suarez. Copied from TV Tropes:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Matthew Sobol is the young, genius programmer head of CyberStorm, one of the world's most successful computer gaming companies. At least until he dies from cancer. However, before dying, he spent a good portion of his prodigious talent and vast fortune designing and building custom hardware and writing a collection of sophisticated computer programs that have been left sitting passive on machines scatted around the Internet. Passive, that is, until one of them reads Sobol's obituary. This program sends triggers to other systems which activate a number of other distributed processes; the Daemon awakes.<br /> <br /> Among its first actions are to kill two of Sobol's coworkers. When they try to forcibly enter his mansion after connecting Sobol with the aforementioned murders, a number of police and FBI agents are maimed or killed by an impressive set of boobytraps, including an autonomous, murderous Humvee that is nearly impervious to everything they can throw at it. The Daemon then frames its actions on a handful of people to cast doubt on its very existence and withdraws from the public eye. It quietly offers certain people in key positions fame and success if they make a deal with the devil, or more accurately, the Daemon. Then, ominously, it goes silent. When it resurfaces, things go downhill. Fast.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It seems too work like a Nascent GM, or Maybe an Angel or Process/Project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T19:44:12-07:00","id":515696,"title":"","content":"Black Mirror is a British tv series reminiscent of the Twilight Zone about the dark side of mixing technology and human nature. The whole show reeks of God Machine Infrastructure and how the God Machine can hijack human infrastructure for its projects.<br /> <br /> Marvel's Daredevil on Netflix is basically the World of Darkness minus the supernatural. Good inspiration for a Vampire chronicle, especially if you consider Wilson Fisk as an Invictus or Carthian Prince.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5700-nuwisha-nutjob","name":"Nuwisha Nutjob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T18:33:19-07:00","id":522745,"title":"","content":"A few off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> Monogatari Series - Spirits and stuff<br /> <br /> The witches from Madoka Magica are also good for spirits of madness/despair and shadowrealm weirdness<br /> <br /> Dog Soldiers - for a mortal's perspective on werewolves<br /> <br /> I, Frankenstein - Promethean (duh)<br /> <br /> The Thing on the Doorstep - Body-thieves from the Immortals book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3355-not-a-platypus","name":"Not a Platypus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3355_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T06:39:33-07:00","id":523130,"title":"","content":"Not a Film/Tv Series or even a Book.. But a Song i can See working for a... Benevolent Beast<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Lu3zmp5gdyU\" target=\"_blank\"> Kirby Krackle: The Day my Powers Arrived </a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T07:36:40-07:00","id":523163,"title":"","content":"Dexter should be required viewing for Promethean and Vampire players.<br /> <br /> Promethean, because the character of Dexter perfectly embodies the idea of not quite being human, not exactly understanding humanity, but trying all the same, and failing as often as not. Particularly, I think he's a perfect example of the Aurum Refinement, imitating humanity in the hopes that one day, he'll be as he acts.<br /> <br /> For Vampire, while the &quot;Dead Emotions&quot; bit is played down quite a bit in 2E, Dexter provides a perfect example for how it would work in practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T07:53:56-07:00","id":523193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/501475-inspirational-movies-and-tv-episodes?p=523163#post523163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dexter should be required viewing for Promethean and Vampire players.<br /> <br /> Promethean, because the character of Dexter perfectly embodies the idea of not quite being human, not exactly understanding humanity, but trying all the same, and failing as often as not. Particularly, I think he's a perfect example of the Aurum Refinement, imitating humanity in the hopes that one day, he'll be as he acts.<br /> <br /> For Vampire, while the &quot;Dead Emotions&quot; bit is played down quite a bit in 2E, Dexter provides a perfect example for how it would work in practice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't forget <i>the need </i>for vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T12:47:04-07:00","id":523588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/501475-inspirational-movies-and-tv-episodes?p=523193#post523193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Don't forget <i>the need </i>for vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Never really thought of it that way, but excellent point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T12:00:06-07:00","id":525764,"title":"","content":"Millennium, for hunter games, especially for those focusing on the VASCU, Precinct 13 or other cop heavy games.<br /> <br /> Persona 4 (not a movie or tv, I know) was instrumental in getting me to protray the communities that chronicles take place in as places that <i>other</i> people live in, and that makes them worth protecting.<br /> <br /> Twin peaks - a small, isolated community that's slightly... off.<br /> <br /> Blue Bloods - not a show I found perfect, but the dynamic between the father (police commissioner) the two brothers (a cowboy cop detective and idealistic patrol cop) and the daughter (the DA). Whenever an investigation comes up the characters often have wildly different vantage points and concerns, which helped me form the organizational politics of the campaigns I run.<br /> <br /> True Detectives<br /> <br /> Orphan Black","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T14:37:53-07:00","id":525959,"title":"","content":"<b>General WoD</b><br /> <br /> Games - GTA Series, Legacy of Kain, Resident Evil, Silent Hill<br /> Film - Blade, Blair Witch Project, The Crow, Dark City, Hellboy, the Matrix, Pan's Labyrinth, Pulp Fiction, Seven, Snatch, and a lifetimes worth of other horror films.<br /> Television - Buffy TVS, Constantine [#saveconstantine], Dead Like Me, Master's of Horror, Fear Itself, Night Gallery, The Outer Limit, Supernatural, Tales from the Crypt, Tales from the Darkside, The Twilight Zone.<br /> <br /> Films like the Blade or the Crow feel like movies where <i>someone</i> on the production staff was was White Wolf gamer. Perhaps more so in the Classic WoD, but the general look and feel of these films present a world that is a somewhat dingier version of the world outside your window.<br /> Horror Anthology series give me ideas for the multitude of strange occurrences and terrors (both mundane and otherwise). And shows like Buffy or Supernatural have so many interesting big bads, mythologies, and monsters of the week that it is hard not to snatch an idea or two. and the films of Guy Ritchie and Quentin Tarantino both teach the lesson that <i>Style Matters</i>. <br /> <br /> <b>Vampire</b><br /> <br /> Film - Casino, Dracula (Bela Lugosi), Fright Night, the Godfather Trilogy, Goodfellas, Interview with a Vampire, Near Dark, New Jack City, Reservoir Dogs, The Usual Suspects<br /> Television - Breaking Bad, Gangland, Kindred:the Embraced, Law and Order: SVU, the Sopranos, True Blood<br /> <br /> My Vampire games owe much to the Crime genre. I see parallels between the All-Night Society and the inner workings of organized crime. I layer those ideas with a nice helping of actual Vampire Movies/TV, with personal favorites being Fright Night, Near Dark, and of course, Bela Lugosi in Dracula.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf</b><br /> <br /> Film - An American Werewolf in London, Colors, Dog Soldiers, Gangs of New York, Glory, Ginger Snaps, Full Metal Jacket,the Howling, Platoon, Spaghetti Westerns, Tombstone, the Warriors<br /> <br /> My werewolf inspirations come mostly from film [I don't see many werewolf themes on tv, or at least on anything I have seen]. The I like war films for the valor and fatalism displayed [great for WtA], while I prefer films about gangs for WtF, for the violence, fast life, and &quot;us against the world&quot; mentality. Both of these genres place a great importance of the unit over the individual, important when running a game about packs. The westerns have these wonderfully majestic, yet somewhat stark and lonely backdrops that always feel appropriate for werewolf games.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T18:16:17-07:00","id":527219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/501475-inspirational-movies-and-tv-episodes?p=525959#post525959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>General WoD</b><br /> <br /> Games - GTA Series, Legacy of Kain, Resident Evil, Silent Hill<br /> Film - Blade, Blair Witch Project, The Crow, Dark City, Hellboy, the Matrix, Pan's Labyrinth, Pulp Fiction, Seven, Snatch, and a lifetimes worth of other horror films.<br /> Television - Buffy TVS, Constantine [#saveconstantine], Dead Like Me, Master's of Horror, Fear Itself, Night Gallery, The Outer Limit, Supernatural, Tales from the Crypt, Tales from the Darkside, The Twilight Zone.<br /> <br /> Films like the Blade or the Crow feel like movies where <i>someone</i> on the production staff was was White Wolf gamer. Perhaps more so in the Classic WoD, but the general look and feel of these films present a world that is a somewhat dingier version of the world outside your window.<br /> Horror Anthology series give me ideas for the multitude of strange occurrences and terrors (both mundane and otherwise). And shows like Buffy or Supernatural have so many interesting big bads, mythologies, and monsters of the week that it is hard not to snatch an idea or two. and the films of Guy Ritchie and Quentin Tarantino both teach the lesson that <i>Style Matters</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire</b><br /> <br /> Film - Casino, Dracula (Bela Lugosi), Fright Night, the Godfather Trilogy, Goodfellas, Interview with a Vampire, Near Dark, New Jack City, Reservoir Dogs, The Usual Suspects<br /> Television - Breaking Bad, Gangland, Kindred:the Embraced, Law and Order: SVU, the Sopranos, True Blood<br /> <br /> My Vampire games owe much to the Crime genre. I see parallels between the All-Night Society and the inner workings of organized crime. I layer those ideas with a nice helping of actual Vampire Movies/TV, with personal favorites being Fright Night, Near Dark, and of course, Bela Lugosi in Dracula.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf</b><br /> <br /> Film - An American Werewolf in London, Colors, Dog Soldiers, Gangs of New York, Glory, Ginger Snaps, Full Metal Jacket,the Howling, Platoon, Spaghetti Westerns, Tombstone, the Warriors<br /> <br /> My werewolf inspirations come mostly from film [I don't see many werewolf themes on tv, or at least on anything I have seen]. The I like war films for the valor and fatalism displayed [great for WtA], while I prefer films about gangs for WtF, for the violence, fast life, and &quot;us against the world&quot; mentality. Both of these genres place a great importance of the unit over the individual, important when running a game about packs. The westerns have these wonderfully majestic, yet somewhat stark and lonely backdrops that always feel appropriate for werewolf games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much like the poster I quoted, crime movies have also influenced my WoD games, especially Vampire. Since I mostly run Requiem and Lost, here's my inspirations for both. I traditionally eschew Gothic and Punk stuff, as well as personal horror, instead going for action-drama instead.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire: The Requiem </b><br /> <br /> Dracula<br /> The Lost Boys<br /> Near Dark<br /> Underworld<br /> The Godfather Trilogy<br /> Goodfellas<br /> Casino<br /> Gangs of New York<br /> American Ninja<br /> Interview With A Vampire<br /> Grand Theft Auto series<br /> Resident Evil series<br /> Mafia II<br /> Dead or Alive series<br /> BloodRayne<br /> Street Fighter series<br /> Final Fantasy VII<br /> The Sopranos<br /> Sons of Anarchy<br /> The Shield<br /> Gangland<br /> Black Lagoon<br /> Hellsing Ultimate<br /> Vampire Hunter D<br /> Fullmetal Alchemist (2003 anime, NOT Brotherhood)<br /> Ghost in the Shell: Stand Alone Complex<br /> <br /> <b>Changeling: The Lost </b><br /> <br /> The Lord of the Rings<br /> A Nightmare on Elm Street<br /> Dungeons &amp; Dragons (specifically the Ravenloft setting)<br /> The Dark Tower<br /> Army Men series<br /> Toy Story<br /> Spirited Away<br /> Jurassic Park<br /> Peter Pan<br /> Anastasia<br /> Final Fantasy VII<br /> Bleach<br /> Silent Hill<br /> The X-Files<br /> InuYasha<br /> Naruto Part I<br /> Sailor Moon<br /> Digimon Adventure<br /> Digimon Tamers<br /> Urotsukidoji<br /> The Elder Scrolls III: Morrowind<br /> Fallout 3<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 05-24-2015, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T20:36:21-07:00","id":527305,"title":"","content":"For <b>Beast</b>: Fight Club, Ferris Bueller's Day Off (under the <a href=\"http://www.slashfilm.com/the-ferris-bueller-fight-club-theory/\" target=\"_blank\">Cameron's Fight Club</a> interpretation), and Foster's Home etc.: Destination Imagination. The first two can show two very different versions of a Beast's Soul running wild, and the last is a perfect example of a big Lair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T07:23:19-07:00","id":527650,"title":"","content":"Teen Wolf is a great werewolf TV show. Yeah, I know it's on MTV, but it's still really good. Lots of weirdness that may be good inspirations for Spirit-realm stuff, particularly the second half of Season 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T00:03:52-07:00","id":530723,"title":"","content":"Penny dreadful.<br /> <br /> All im saying<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T09:25:50-07:00","id":531086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephraim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/501475-inspirational-movies-and-tv-episodes?p=530723#post530723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Penny dreadful.<br /> <br /> All im saying<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've heard some decent things about the show. But I'm not sure I should devote any time to it. Is it that good of a show?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T09:46:47-07:00","id":531095,"title":"","content":"Here to second Penny Dreadful. It has its teeth firmly in pretty much all the World of Darkness templates and is fantastic. Especially love the Frankenstein/Promethean elements of the show, since that has so rarely been done convincingly or so well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T10:06:48-07:00","id":531104,"title":"","content":"It's got some nice writing. The writers utterly fail when it comes to pacing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T02:38:48-07:00","id":531810,"title":"","content":"Dude of Legend: I can only speak for myself, but this show is for me the best TV i can get nowadays. I have completely fallen off the GoT-Wagon.<br /> PD is not perfect, but I like it that way. It has a great cast, very good writing.<br /> Every single episode could be a story in World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Also: mini-series I kind of liked: Residue. It has a lot of faults, but some of the scenes give me ton of inspiration for WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T11:47:34-07:00","id":532092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephraim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/501475-inspirational-movies-and-tv-episodes?p=530723#post530723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Penny dreadful.<br /> <br /> All im saying<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Victorian Hunter, all I'm saying... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T14:19:29-07:00","id":532270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephraim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/501475-inspirational-movies-and-tv-episodes?p=531810#post531810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude of Legend: I can only speak for myself, but this show is for me the best TV i can get nowadays. I have completely fallen off the GoT-Wagon.<br /> PD is not perfect, but I like it that way. It has a great cast, very good writing.<br /> Every single episode could be a story in World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll give it a chance this weekend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T06:46:06-07:00","id":533141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/501475-inspirational-movies-and-tv-episodes?p=532092#post532092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Victorian Hunter, all I'm saying... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. :-)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum