"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T09:53:51-08:00","id":774877,"title":"","content":"Mr Robot and Person of Interest are my ultimate Demon shows.<br /> <br /> Hannibal is my ultimate Beast show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T21:29:19-08:00","id":775786,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://imdb.com/title/tt1767354/\" target=\"_blank\">Odd Thomas</a> is a great movie for a ghost-based campaign, especially if you're playing psychics or a low power Sin-Eater","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7034-momotato","name":"momotato","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T22:25:32-08:00","id":775810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>momotato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/501475-inspirational-movies-and-tv-episodes?p=775786#post775786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://imdb.com/title/tt1767354/\" target=\"_blank\">Odd Thomas</a> is a great movie for a ghost-based campaign, especially if you're playing psychics or a low power Sin-Eater</div> </div> </div> </div>I Definately agree. Also works well with Hunter: VSCU as well, dealing with the Budding Slashers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;I am a daydreamer and a Night thinker.&quot;~</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1820-nightout","name":"Nightout","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T11:21:28-08:00","id":776111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/501475-inspirational-movies-and-tv-episodes?p=771216#post771216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt2357547/?ref_=fn_al_tt_1\" target=\"_blank\">Jessica Jones</a> has a great example of Dominate, and how the interpretation can matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also good for Changeling. While Jessica's powers did not come from Kilgrave the trauma she experienced at his hands shaped every aspect of her life thereafter. Not to mention the endless paranoia and inability to trust anyone in the face a seemingly all powerful entity out to retake you as captive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T13:37:48-08:00","id":776178,"title":"","content":"Sleepy Hollow's vibe is a little... schlocky, but it's got tons of Hunter material, and at times some really extraordinary visuals. Also if Fox ever gets around to releasing the music as an album, I'll be using a bunch of it as neutral background music.<br /> <br /> The Sinister movies do a really <i>amazing </i>job at showing just how alien ghosts can be, visually and behaviorally.<br /> <br /> Gravity Falls is a fun example of a non-Splat-dominated WoD town with a weirdness-distilling agency. Also, the characters are generally very good people, but have some understated but <i>serious </i>disfunctional issues with each other that do a great job of showing that just because you're part of an (actually) loving family doesn't mean you can't exhibit seriously divisive and toxic behavior on the down-low. I've personally started playing with it as part of a setting, as a kind of supernatural demilitarized zone with a reputation for quietly and repeatedly chewing up and spitting out enough vampires, werewolves, and changelings that the only ones who go are assumed to be crazy or leveraged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 11-28-2015, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T17:52:03-08:00","id":776310,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0810788/\" target=\"_blank\">Burn Notice</a> for Demon. A show about a former spy who has had all his ties to his agency cut. While we can assume the CIA is at least slightly more benevolent than the God Machine Michael Westen's relentless efforts to get his old job back can all too easily be mapped onto an Integrator. His homemade spycraft is potentially useful to any kind of PC operating in legally questionable territory but especially fits into Demon's MO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T18:29:09-08:00","id":776348,"title":"","content":"When it comes to video games, I think Sang Froid: Tales of Werewolves is a great inspiration for a dark eras hunter game set in the rural 1800s (plus the soundtrack is AMAZING! It's all traditional French Canadian folk music (because it's set in 1800s Quebec) ). It really manages to show the amount of planning it takes for mortals to take down a group of supernaturals (and shows how it's useful to have a couple supernatural allies to help out.)<br /> <br /> <br /> and besides, the concept of lumberjacks VS werewolves is golden on it's own.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T10:13:40-08:00","id":777813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/501475-inspirational-movies-and-tv-episodes?p=527650#post527650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Teen Wolf is a great werewolf TV show. Yeah, I know it's on MTV, but it's still really good. Lots of weirdness that may be good inspirations for Spirit-realm stuff, particularly the second half of Season 3.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree. It makes for a pretty great Werewolf/Mage crossover setting, since it has a ready made 'central mystery' and packs have an enshrined role for human magic users.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T20:26:07-08:00","id":778077,"title":"","content":"I know Marvel's Daredevil was mentioned once before, but I want to point out that it's also perfect for Beasts, with the Daredevil as an Eshmaki Nemesis opposing Fisk, the Anakim Tyrant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T20:35:46-08:00","id":778082,"title":"","content":"I thought the depiction of his senses, not in the 'I can see just not the fine details,' but him hearing and smelling and even feeling things was pretty good for Werewolf and their enhanced sensory powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T10:22:09-08:00","id":778435,"title":"","content":"I recently realized something crazy.<br /> <br /> The X-Men are a really good inspiration for W:tF.<br /> <br /> I know it sounds crazy but actually think about it:<ul><li>They are an insular family-type group with a shared origin but varied supernatural abilities.</li> <li>They have Xavier's school as territory.</li> <li>Xavier himself could be their totem.</li> <li>They deal with others of their kind that are fanatic in the idea that they are superior to regular humans (The Brotherhood of Mutants, The Hellfire Club, Apocalypse and his Horsemen).</li> <li>They deal with hunters (The Friends of Humanity, Bolivar Trask and the Sentinels).</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T14:04:48-08:00","id":778583,"title":"","content":"I now cannot stop seeing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T12:14:44-08:00","id":779160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_containe