enoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T03:38:51-08:00","id":1026957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/501475-inspirational-movies-and-tv-episodes?p=1026806#post1026806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">nothing against Lovecraft, but I don't think he produced any TV or Movies <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. That said maybe someone has produced TV or movies based on his writing that I don't know about.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a bunch of movies based on his works. Maybe thirty to forty in total, but only a few of them are faithful adaptations. The two most faithful are made by a fan society. Call of Cthulhu (2005) and The Whisperer in Darkness (2011). Both made to simulate older film styles, to varying degrees of success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T15:02:08-07:00","id":1091290,"title":"","content":"Awesome song, awesome video, also inspiration. The 'human spider' form of the wolf is especially creepy in a way that I associate with CofD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://vimeo.com/214208482\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i.vimeocdn.com/filter/overlay?src0=https%3A%2F%2Fi.vimeocdn.com%2Fvideo%2F630639462-d9a5941a25c088593418a1f3b2d26eb657c5e7ad8cb4cb2338978bdd92fc8e87-d_1280x720&amp;src1=https%3A%2F%2Ff.vimeocdn.com%2Fimages_v6%2Fshare%2Fplay_icon_overlay.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://vimeo.com/214208482\" target=\"_blank\"> SIAMES - The Wolf </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://vimeo.com/214208482\" target=\"_blank\"> https://vimeo.com/214208482 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> &ldquo;The Wolf&rdquo; is an animated Music Video for argentinian band SIAMES. Produced independently by Buenos Aires based studio Rudo Company, every frame has&hellip; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sorry for the thread necromancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T18:52:36-07:00","id":1091376,"title":"","content":"Check out Halfworlds, which is an original series by HBO Asia. The premise involves gang wars and criminal underworld dealings by a secret society descended from the demons and supernatural creatures of Southeast Asian folklore. Season 1 was set in Jakarta, and Season 2 is in Bangkok.<br /> <br /> The tone is visibly dark and slightly cyberpunk, set against the backdrop of the megapolises of the region. This could easily be Demon, Changeling, or Vampire. One of the pluses for me is that its mythology is Eastern, which is a rare thing when the usually tropes are drawn from Western folklore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T20:12:20-07:00","id":1092641,"title":"","content":"<b>Changeling:</b> <i>Little Nightmares</i> is a game that's come out recently. It's an escape from a Durance, pure and simple. She's an Ogre, by the way.<br /> <b>Deviant:</b> <i>Cybersix</i>.<br /> <b>Hunter:</b> <i>Roswell Conspiracies: Aliens, Myths, and Legends</i> is great for pulp-y Conspiracy level play.<br /> <b>Innocents:</b> <i><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JHZKYo_sfGg\" target=\"_blank\">Mona the Vampire</a></i>. What?<br /> <b>Mortals:</b> <i>Detentionaire</i> and <i>Delta State</i> are great inspiration for a Mortals game. Detentionaire is pretty schlock-y, granted, and takes a dive after the first season or so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T00:19:25-07:00","id":1092684,"title":"","content":"Geist: Brimstone tv series or could be Demon. Sadly it was cut short after 13 episodes<br /> Mage: Carnivale also cut after two seasons with proves that we can't have nice things <br /> Vampire: John Wick 1 and 2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T17:39:05-07:00","id":1095303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/501475-inspirational-movies-and-tv-episodes#post501475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I decided to start this thread because I like finding new things that fit within the vein of WoD, and because I've had problems finding certain aspects of WoD in Movies/TV in the past (Specifically Werewolf the Forsaken 1e when dealing with Spirits and the Shadow realm).[/LIST]</div> </div> </div> </div>The spirit world of Forsaken? Evil Dead (2013), The Exorcist (1973), The Exorcist 3 (1990), The Possession (2012), Hellraiser (1987), Prince of Darkness (1987), Fallen (1998), Children of the Corn (84/09), The Ring (2002) - really a lot of J-Horror stuff draws on the idea of hostile spiritual forces. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T20:52:33-07:00","id":1098337,"title":"","content":"Joe Ledger Series: This a great inspiration book for demon, hunter, and even vampire.<br /> Book 1:Patient Zero (2009) - This Book Covers Joe Ledger Fighting off terrorist group that found away to make zombies.<br /> Book 2:The Dragon Factory (2010) - Joe Ledger and the (Department of Military Sciences) go up against genetic super soldiers<br /> Book 3:The King of Plagues (2011) - Joe Ledger and the DMS Fights a Global Conspiracy group Known as the 7 kings akin to the Illuminati<br /> Book 4: Assassins Code (2012) - He Fights Vampires in the middle east that stole nukes<br /> Book 5:Extinction Machine (2013) - He Fights the men in black and an alien conspiracy (AKA God-Machine)<br /> Book 6:Code Zero (2014) - Joe Ledger Fights a Genius Hacker using the zombie from the first book to try and destroy the world.<br /> Book 7:Predator One (2015) - This time a terrorist group use a Quantum computer to take control of the U.S military infrastructure<br /> Book 8:Kill Switch (2016) - This time Joe Fights The God-Machine. Yes Their is a God-Machine in this book<br /> Book 9: Dogs of War (2017) - I have not read this one yet but it says. A freelance terrorist uses the latest generation of robot dogs to deliver WMDs into cities across America. Ultra-realistic robots in the sex industry are used to spread designer plagues<br /> <br /> This book series is a great wealth of ideas for any GM<br /> <br /> Sorry I thought this thread was for Media not only TV and Movies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","user":"Basic","date":". 05-30-2017, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}